{%- comment -%}
  Toolbar gender quick-filter buttons (replaces the old hardcoded, unwired
  `.c5dla-toolbar .genders` text).

  Finds the Shopify "target-gender" taxonomy filter in `results.filters`
  and renders one button per value, plus a permanent "All genders" first -
  renders nothing if the collection has no gender filter at all.

  These are a quick-filter shortcut for the SAME checkbox
  snippets/5dla_filter-sort-drawer.liquid renders, not a parallel
  mechanism: client/ver_2_0/js/modules/filter-sort.js's
  `filter:filterByGender` listener finds the matching `label[title="..."]`
  checkbox and fires a real `change` on it, going through the normal
  AJAX path (and re-rendering these buttons' `active` state from the
  response).

  One-way, not a toggle: clicking a gender button always turns that
  gender ON (never off again by re-clicking) - only "All genders" clears
  it, since filter-sort.js unchecks every gender input first, then
  (re)checks only the clicked one.

  `results` (required): same collection object passed to
  snippets/5dla_filter-sort-drawer.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gender_filter = nil
  for filter in results.filters
    if filter.param_name contains 'target-gender'
      assign gender_filter = filter
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if gender_filter -%}
  <div class="genders">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="{% if gender_filter.active_values.size == 0 %}active{% endif %}"
      data-c5dla-gender-button
      data-gender-title=""
    >
      {{ 'products.facets.all' | t }} genders
    </button>
    {%- for value in gender_filter.values -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="{% if value.active %}active{% endif %}"
        data-c5dla-gender-button
        data-gender-title="{{ value.label | escape }}"
      >
        {{ value.label | escape }}
      </button>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
